<title>HONG KONG: Sum Cheong 1995/96 net loss HK$67.76 mln.</title>
<headline>Sum Cheong 1995/96 net loss HK$67.76 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   70.0 loss  vs 29.0 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  78.08 loss vs 0.84 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    67.76 loss vs 27.63 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,329.36   vs 1,077.59</p>
<p>    Company name		 Sum Cheong International Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Sum Cheong International is a holding company with units engaged in trading, construction, mining and manufacturing.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on write-down of an investment in an associated company to its net realisable value and deferred expenditure for a mining project and fees for special accountants' reports and a management change-over.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs 10 H.K. cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
